      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1761490000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "AWS manages servers; you manage code/config",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AWS manages servers; you manage code/config",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "p4-0039",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 1285,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 245,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 429,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 507,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1761490000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "EC2 OFTEN FITS\n• Long-running API or worker\n• OS-level control / custom runtime\n• Steady baseline capacity may be economical\n• You own instance patching, capacity and process health\n• Usually uses a load balancer and Auto Scaling",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "EC2 OFTEN FITS\n• Long-running API or worker\n• OS-level control / custom runtime\n• Steady baseline capacity may be economical\n• You own instance patching, capacity and process health\n• Usually uses a load balancer and Auto Scaling",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "p4-0040",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 1285,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 245,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 440,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 520,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1761490000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "LAMBDA OFTEN FITS\n• Event-driven, bursty, bounded tasks\n• Less server-management overhead\n• Pay per requests + execution/resources (pricing rules apply)\n• Design for timeouts, retries, cold starts and concurrency\n• Protect databases from connection/concurrency spikes",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "LAMBDA OFTEN FITS\n• Event-driven, bursty, bounded tasks\n• Less server-management overhead\n• Pay per requests + execution/resources (pricing rules apply)\n• Design for timeouts, retries, cold starts and concurrency\n• Protect databases from connection/concurrency spikes",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "p4-0041",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 1570,
      "width": 1580,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#3e6a3a",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 451,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 533,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1761490000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "BOTH: servers still exist; both need security, observability, quotas/capacity planning, durable state, and safe handling of retries. Lambda handlers should be idempotent when events can repeat.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BOTH: servers still exist; both need security, observability, quotas/capacity planning, durable state, and safe handling of retries. Lambda handlers should be idempotent when events can repeat.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
